# Interactive request file for testing the running adapter from Visual Studio.
#
# 1. Start the app with the "Container (Dockerfile)" launch profile (F5).
# 2. Visual Studio publishes a random host port. Set @port below to the mapped port, which is shown in
#    the Containers window (Ports tab) or in the address bar when the Swagger UI opens.
# 3. Click "Send request" above any request below.
#
# @auth is the base64 of "<username>:<password>" and must match I3X_BASIC_AUTH_USERNAME /
# I3X_BASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD in Properties/launchSettings.json. To regenerate it after changing the
# credentials, run in PowerShell:
#   [Convert]::ToBase64String([Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes("i3x:changeit"))

@host = http://localhost
@port = 8080
@baseUrl = {{host}}:{{port}}/v1

# base64 of "i3x:changeit"
@auth = aTN4OmNoYW5nZWl0

### Health / capabilities - the only endpoint that does not require authentication.
GET {{baseUrl}}/info
Accept: application/json

### Unauthenticated data request - expected to fail with 401 and a WWW-Authenticate challenge.
GET {{baseUrl}}/objects
Accept: application/json

### Namespaces discovered from the InfluxDB metadata measurement.
GET {{baseUrl}}/namespaces
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

### Root objects of the ISA-95 hierarchy.
GET {{baseUrl}}/objects?root=true
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

### All objects, including their metadata.
GET {{baseUrl}}/objects?includeMetadata=true
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

### Object types (one per distinct OPC UA data type per namespace).
GET {{baseUrl}}/objecttypes
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

### Relationship types (static, well-known OPC UA reference types).
GET {{baseUrl}}/relationshiptypes
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

### Verify gzip is honored, as the i3X spec requires.
GET {{baseUrl}}/objects
Accept: application/json
Accept-Encoding: gzip
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

### Children of an object. Replace the elementId with one returned by /objects.
POST {{baseUrl}}/objects/related
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

{
  "elementIds": ["<elementId>"],
  "relationshipType": "HasComponent"
}

### Current value of one or more objects. Replace the elementIds with real ones.
POST {{baseUrl}}/objects/value
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

{
  "elementIds": ["<subject>::<variableName>"]
}

### Historical values. startTime and endTime are mandatory RFC 3339 timestamps.
POST {{baseUrl}}/objects/history
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

{
  "elementIds": ["<subject>::<variableName>"],
  "startTime": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "endTime": "2034-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}

### Create a subscription; returns the subscriptionId used by the calls below.
POST {{baseUrl}}/subscriptions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

{}

### Register elements on a subscription. Replace <subscriptionId> with the id returned above.
POST {{baseUrl}}/subscriptions/<subscriptionId>/register
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

{
  "elementIds": ["<subject>::<variableName>"]
}

### Poll for changes since the last sync.
POST {{baseUrl}}/subscriptions/<subscriptionId>/sync
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

{}

### Server-sent events stream of changes.
GET {{baseUrl}}/subscriptions/<subscriptionId>/stream
Accept: text/event-stream
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}
